<title>USA: GOLF-AUSTRALIA TO HOST 1998 PRESIDENTS CUP.</title>
<headline>GOLF-AUSTRALIA TO HOST 1998 PRESIDENTS CUP.</headline>
<dateline>PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Florida 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The next Presidents Cup international team golf competition will be staged in Australia in 1998, the U.S. PGA Tour announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Australian host city for the biennial match play event, in which a U.S. team plays against an International squad, has not yet been determined.</p>
<p>The United States won the inaugural Presidents Cup in 1994 and retained the title this past September.</p>
</text>
